# .env.example -- template for the training runbook's secrets.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then paste your values into .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# .env is gitignored. submit.sh and the subset Makefile targets source it
# automatically (`set -a; source .env; set +a`); for a bare condor_submit
# run that line yourself first. Values are quoted on purpose: the NYU URLs
# contain & and ?, which an unquoted shell assignment treats as operators.
#
# NEVER paste any of these into a .sub file. They reach the job through
# HTCondor getenv from your shell, so they show up in the job ClassAd
# (condor_q -l), readable by you and CHTC admins only.

# --- Weights & Biases --------------------------------------------------------
# From https://wandb.ai/authorize. Rotate the key that sits in the old
# Research/inpainting.sub git history before using any key here.
# Absent -> submit.sh refuses unless OFFLINE=1 (logs offline, `wandb sync` later).
WANDB_API_KEY=''
# Optional: your W&B username or team. Blank = your default entity.
WANDB_ENTITY=''

# --- fastMRI knee train split (NYU) ------------------------------------------
# NYU ships the train split as five batches, knee_multicoil_train_batch_0..4
# (~91 GB each). Paste the presigned URL for knee_multicoil_train_batch_0.tar.xz
# from the approval email exactly, query string included (the text between
# the quotes on the line ending in `--output knee_multicoil_train_batch_0.tar.xz`).
# It is a credential and expires ~90 days after issue. Only subset_train.sub uses it (README section 3b).
FASTMRI_TRAIN_URL=''
